      "code": "Tokenize(tokens, begin, tempAllocator);",
      "note": "This is the first project statement that converts the raw witness bytes into parser state used by the bug. For this exact witness, `Tokenize` creates `KEY(\"Fbx\"), OPEN_BRACKET, KEY(\"\\xFF\"), OPEN_BRACKET, CLOSE_BRACKET`, leaving the outer `Fbx` scope unterminated.",
      "kind": "source"
    },
    {
      "file": "code/AssetLib/FBX/FBXParser.cpp",
      "function": "Assimp::FBX::Scope::Scope",
      "line": null,
      "code": "if (n == nullptr) {\n    if (topLevel) {\n        elements.insert(ElementMap::value_type(str, element));\n        return;\n    }\n    delete element;\n    ParseError(\"unexpected end of file\",parser.LastToken());\n}",
      "note": "When the outer scope reaches this branch on the witness, `n == nullptr` because the inner empty scope consumed the only closing brace, and `topLevel == false` because the scope was created from the first `{` after `Fbx`. `FBXParser.h` defines `delete_Element(_p) (_p)->~Element()`, and `Scope::~Scope()` later destroys stored elements with that helper, so this EOF branch is the ownership-violating special case fixed by the patch.",
      "kind": "root_cause_function"
    },
